From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: McKack <4465550+McKack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:33:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvapi: add D3D12, DRS, D3D11 device creation and GPU/display
 lookup functions

Adds 36 functions DXMT's NVAPI did not have, with behaviour adapted from
dxvk-nvapi (MIT, notice kept in nvapi_ported.cpp). DRS now opens a session
instead of failing, so games get past their profile lookup. D3D12 calls
report what DXMT supports: no NVIDIA shader extensions, no raytracing caps,
Reflex accepted and ignored. GPU and display lookups use DXMT's existing
handles (Metal registry IDs, HMONITORs) and PCI IDs come from DXGI.
